      proofName: "Verification of the axioms with names", proofYear: 1963, proofWho: "Cohen",
      formula: String.raw`M \subseteq M[G] \models \mathrm{ZFC},\quad \mathrm{Ord}^{M[G]} = \mathrm{Ord}^M`,
      text: "If M is a countable transitive model of ZFC and G is generic over M, then M[G] is a countable transitive model of ZFC with the same ordinals as M; it is the smallest such model containing M and G.",
